problem:
Problem description
- There is a single planning decision for transporting a required amount of goods from an origin to a destination using a finite set of transportation modes $$\mathcal{M}$$.
- The modes include one primary mode and two alternative physically demanding modes, with the alternative modes forming a subset $$\mathcal{B} \subseteq \mathcal{M}$$.
- Each mode $$m \in \mathcal{M}$$ has a per-trip carrying capacity $$q_m$$ and a per-trip pollution amount $$e_m$$.
- The total demand to be transported is the parameter $$D$$.
- The total pollution generated by all trips must not exceed the pollution limit $$E^{\max}$$.
- The primary mode has a minimum-use requirement of at least $$L$$ trips.
- At most one mode from the physically demanding subset $$\mathcal{B}$$ may be selected for use.
- The planning goal is to minimize total pollution while still transporting at least the required amount of goods.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_m$$: the number of trips assigned to transportation mode $$m \in \mathcal{M}$$.
  - $$y_m$$: a binary usage indicator for mode $$m \in \mathcal{B}$$, showing whether that mode is selected for use.
  - $$z$$: the total pollution generated by the transportation plan.

Input Format
{
  "sets": {
    "M": {
      "description": "Set of transportation modes, indexed by $$m \in \\mathcal{M}$$",
      "elements": "Symbolic labels for all available modes"
    },
    "B": {
      "description": "Subset of physically demanding modes, indexed by $$m \in \\mathcal{B} \\subseteq \\mathcal{M}$$",
      "elements": "Symbolic labels for the restricted alternative modes"
    }
  },
  "parameters": {
    "D": {
      "description": "Total amount of goods that must be transported",
      "type": "nonnegative scalar"
    },
    "q": {
      "description": "Per-trip carrying capacity for each mode",
      "shape": "vector over $$\\mathcal{M}$$",
      "meaning": "$$q_m$$ is the amount transported by one trip using mode $$m$$"
    },
    "e": {
      "description": "Per-trip pollution for each mode",
      "shape": "vector over $$\\mathcal{M}$$",
      "meaning": "$$e_m$$ is the pollution generated by one trip using mode $$m$$"
    },
    "E_max": {
      "description": "Maximum allowed total pollution",
      "type": "nonnegative scalar"
    },
    "L": {
      "description": "Minimum number of trips required for the primary mode",
      "type": "nonnegative integer"
    },
    "M_primary": {
      "description": "The designated primary transportation mode",
      "type": "single element of $$\\mathcal{M}$$"
    }
  },
  "decision_variables": {
    "x": {
      "description": "Number of trips assigned to each mode",
      "shape": "vector over $$\\mathcal{M}$$",
      "type": "nonnegative integer"
    },
    "y": {
      "description": "Mode-selection indicators for restricted modes",
      "shape": "vector over $$\\mathcal{B}$$",
      "type": "binary"
    }
  },
  "objective": {
    "description": "Minimize total pollution generated by all transportation trips"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "solution": {
    "x": {
      "description": "Trip counts by transportation mode",
      "shape": "vector over $$\\mathcal{M}$$",
      "type": "nonnegative integer"
    },
    "y": {
      "description": "Selection indicators for the physically demanding modes",
      "shape": "vector over $$\\mathcal{B}$$",
      "type": "binary"
    },
    "total_transported": {
      "description": "Total amount of goods transported",
      "type": "nonnegative scalar"
    },
    "total_pollution": {
      "description": "Total pollution produced by the chosen transportation plan",
      "type": "nonnegative scalar"
    }
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "sets": {
    "M": ["horse", "bicycle", "handcart"],
    "B": ["bicycle", "handcart"]
  },
  "parameters": {
    "D": 1000,
    "q": {
      "horse": 55,
      "bicycle": 30,
      "handcart": 40
    },
    "e": {
      "horse": 80,
      "bicycle": 0,
      "handcart": 0
    },
    "E_max": 1000,
    "L": 8,
    "M_primary": "horse"
  }
}
